  "id": "COMPOUND:41593 - PROTEIN:4968",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound (2R,3S,4S,5R,6R)-2-(hydroxymethyl)-6-[(E,1S)-3-[(1R,3S,6S)-3-hydroxy-1,5,5-trimethyl-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-6-yl]-1-methyl-allyloxy]tetrahydropyran-3,4,5-triol and the protein ZR-75-1. This relationship is mediated through the enzyme CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is targeted by multiple compounds in the evidence. The compound appears to inhibit this enzyme, and the enzyme is in turn targeted by several other molecules, including 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan. These findings suggest a complex network of interactions where the compound may act as a modulator of the enzyme, potentially influencing the function of ZR-75-1. The evidence supports a mechanistic pathway involving enzyme inhibition, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
